.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH postar-completions 1  "completions " 
.SH NAME
postar\-completions \- Outputs shell completions to stdout.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpostar completions\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISHELL\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
This command outputs shell completions to stdout. It can be used either in the respective 
shell rc files at startup or just as a one\-time command.
.PP
Here is an example of how it would be used for the zsh shell:
.PP
    eval "$(postar completions zsh)" &> /dev/null
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fISHELL\fR>

.br
[\fIpossible values: \fRzsh, fish, bash]
